    expectedAnswer: "Layered Architecture separates an application into explicit levels such as presentation, application/domain logic, and infrastructure. The key benefit is that responsibilities are easier to locate and dependencies can be constrained instead of allowing every part of the system to call everything else directly.",
    deepExplanation: "Step 1 — Understand the architecture principle.\n\nStep 1 — Define a small dependency boundary.\n\nWITHOUT BUILT-IN / CORE:\n```ts\ninterface UserRepository {\n  findName(id: string): string | null;\n}\n\nfunction createUserService(repository: UserRepository) {\n  return {\n    getDisplayName(id: string): string {\n      const name = repository.findName(id);\n\n      if (name === null) {\n        throw new Error(\"User not found\");\n      }\n\n      return name.trim();\n    },\n  };\n}\n```\n\nStep 2 — Infrastructure implements the stable contract.\n\nWITH BUILT-IN / platform example:\n```ts\ninterface UserRepository {\n  findName(id: string): string | null;\n}\n\nfunction createUserService(repository: UserRepository) {\n  return {\n    getDisplayName(id: string): string {\n      const name = repository.findName(id);\n      if (name === null) throw new Error(\"User not found\");\n      return name.trim();\n    },\n  };\n}\n\nconst repository: UserRepository = {\n  findName(id) {\n    const users = new Map([\n      [\"1\", \"Rasik\"],\n      [\"2\", \"Asha\"],\n    ]);\n\n    return users.get(id) ?? null;\n  },\n};\n\nconst service = createUserService(repository);\n\nconsole.log(service.getDisplayName(\"1\"));\n```\n\nStep 3 — UI depends on the service rather than directly knowing storage details.\n\nExample:\nUI → Application service → Repository interface → API/storage.\n\nBenefits:\n- Clear ownership.\n- Easier unit testing.\n- Lower accidental coupling.\n\nTrade-off:\nMore layers mean more files and indirection. For a tiny app, this can become unnecessary overhead.\n\nStep 5 — Senior interview takeaway:\nExplain what changes this boundary protects, what it costs, and why it is justified.",
