    expectedAnswer: "Onion Architecture emphasizes concentric dependency boundaries: domain rules remain at the center, while application services surround them and infrastructure/UI remain on the outside. The important rule is that outer details depend on inner policies rather than the reverse.",
    deepExplanation: "Step 1 — Understand the architecture principle.\n\nStep 1 — Put a stable domain rule at the center.\n\nWITHOUT BUILT-IN / CORE:\n```ts\nclass Money {\n  constructor(\n    readonly amount: number,\n    readonly currency: string,\n  ) {\n    if (!Number.isFinite(amount)) {\n      throw new Error(\"Invalid amount\");\n    }\n  }\n\n  add(other: Money): Money {\n    if (other.currency !== this.currency) {\n      throw new Error(\"Currency mismatch\");\n    }\n\n    return new Money(this.amount + other.amount, this.currency);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nStep 2 — Application code can orchestrate the domain.\n\nWITH BUILT-IN / plain TypeScript orchestration:\n```ts\nclass Money {\n  constructor(\n    readonly amount: number,\n    readonly currency: string,\n  ) {\n    if (!Number.isFinite(amount)) throw new Error(\"Invalid amount\");\n  }\n\n  add(other: Money): Money {\n    if (other.currency !== this.currency) {\n      throw new Error(\"Currency mismatch\");\n    }\n\n    return new Money(this.amount + other.amount, this.currency);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction calculateTotal(\n  price: Money,\n  tax: Money,\n): Money {\n  return price.add(tax);\n}\n\nconst total = calculateTotal(\n  new Money(100, \"INR\"),\n  new Money(18, \"INR\"),\n);\n```\n\nStep 3 — Infrastructure such as APIs or databases stays outside the domain.\n\nInterview takeaway:\nThe center should not import React, fetch, browser storage, database drivers, or other outer details.\n\nStep 5 — Senior interview takeaway:\nExplain what changes this boundary protects, what it costs, and why it is justified.",
